{"name":"Hot Sauce","hex":"#ab4f41","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot sauce","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any liquid spicy condiment or cooking ingredient made from chili peppers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_sauce"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hot Sauce (Jessy J album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Sauce is the third album by smooth jazz saxophonist Jessy J, released on September 6, 2011. It debuted at No. 1 on the Billboard Jazz chart. The album features guest performances by Saunders Sermons, Paul Brown, Joe Sample, Harvey Mason, and Ray Parker Jr."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/87/Jessy_J_-_Hot_Sauce.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Sauce_(Jessy_J_album)","wikidata":"Q5910337"},{"title":"Hot Sauce (NCT Dream album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Sauce is the first studio album by South Korean boy band NCT Dream, the third sub-unit of the South Korean boy band NCT. It was released on May 10, 2021, through SM Entertainment. Following their previous EP, Reload, this album marks NCT Dream's first release to feature back as a seven-member unit following the return of Mark from the termination of the age-based graduation system that was operated in the group. Hot Sauce is one of the best-selling albums in South Korea."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8b/Hot_Sauce_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Sauce_(NCT_Dream_album)","wikidata":"Q106795747"},{"title":"Hot sauce","blocks":[{"text":"Hot sauce is a type of condiment, seasoning, or salsa made from chili peppers and other ingredients. Many commercial varieties of mass-produced hot sauce exist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Fermented_hot_sauce.jpg/330px-Fermented_hot_sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_sauce","wikidata":"Q522171"},{"title":"Sauce","blocks":[{"text":"In cooking, a sauce is a liquid, cream, or semi-solid food, served on or used in preparing other foods. Most sauces are not normally consumed by themselves; they add flavour, texture, and visual appeal to a dish. Sauce is a French word probably from the post-classical Latin salsa, derived from the classical salsus 'salted'. Possibly the oldest recorded European sauce is garum, the fish sauce used by the Ancient Romans, while doubanjiang, the Chinese soy bean paste, is mentioned in Rites of Zhou 20."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lunch_sauces.jpg/330px-Lunch_sauces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauce","wikidata":"Q178359"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/NCT_Dream_Hello_Future.jpg/250px-NCT_Dream_Hello_Future.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4f/NCT_Dream_Hello_Future.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/4f/NCT_Dream_Hello_Future.jpg/250px-NCT_Dream_Hello_Future.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANCT_Dream_Hello_Future.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/All_kinds_of_hot_sauce.jpg/500px-All_kinds_of_hot_sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/All_kinds_of_hot_sauce.jpg/1280px-All_kinds_of_hot_sauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Al